cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'If you use this software, please cite it as below.'
type: software
title: 'SMILES — structure ⇄ notation conversion, search and exercises'
abstract: "A web application and service for the SMILES chemical line notation. It converts between drawn structures and SMILES in both directions, one at a time or ten thousand at a time, reads and writes SDF, searches a user-supplied set of structures by substructure or SMARTS, and teaches the notation through a guided tutorial, a printable cheatsheet and graded exercises that a teacher can hand out as a link. All chemistry runs in the browser on openchemlib, so no structure ever leaves the visitor's machine."
